{"id": "EUVD-2026-32889", "enisaUuid": "eb566746-0902-338f-bb01-9e15f73a4df6", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndm-verity-fec: fix reading parity bytes split across blocks (take 3)\n\nfec_decode_bufs() assumes that the parity bytes of the first RS codeword\nit decodes are never split across parity blocks.\n\nThis assumption is false.  Consider v->fec->block_size == 4096 &&\nv->fec->roots == 17 && fio->nbufs == 1, for example.  In that case, each\ncall to fec_decode_bufs() consumes v->fec->roots * (fio->nbufs <<\nDM_VERITY_FEC_BUF_RS_BITS) = 272 parity bytes.\n\nConsidering that the parity data for each message block starts on a\nblock boundary, the byte alignment in the parity data will iterate\nthrough 272*i mod 4096 until the 3 parity blocks have been consumed.  On\nthe 16th call (i=15), the alignment will be 4080 bytes into the first\nblock.  Only 16 bytes remain in that block, but 17 parity bytes will be\nneeded.  The code reads out-of-bounds from the parity block buffer.\n\nFortunately this doesn't normally happen, since it can occur only for\ncertain non-default values of fec_roots *and* when the maximum number of\nbuffers couldn't be allocated due to low memory.  For example with\nblock_size=4096 only the following cases are affected:\n\n    fec_roots=17: nbufs in [1, 3, 5, 15]\n    fec_roots=19: nbufs in [1, 229]\n    fec_roots=21: nbufs in [1, 3, 5, 13, 15, 39, 65, 195]\n    fec_roots=23: nbufs in [1, 89]\n\nRegardless, fix it by refactoring how the parity blocks are read.", "datePublished": "2026-05-28T09:35:45", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:41:19", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/03348b440f69417dc3a3c71d8271cff6b05f67fb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dac69d1b76049d7e5f565089a6a7f4502a85b9de", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d47281b9a4472cfd73122393e79fbe76b651e46a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3d1b4e2d8ac0a1a1390a117f61ce0ca1c47e3bcb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/430a05cb926f6bdf53e81460a2c3a553257f3f61"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-46130", "GHSA-6hvc-rwfc-mp4j"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0c96f24f-2231-3e67-972c-26b1a78f7c00", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "12caa73a28f0ae147ec0356b45091edf2462462b <03348b440f69417dc3a3c71d8271cff6b05f67fb"}, {"id": "139c76c6-3589-3e88-a092-638aa5cc5ff1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6bc6ee31113b05db605694491bdeb2b1730142f1"}, {"id": "2685ba52-731d-3b6c-b9a3-733aa9d1371e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "2a0e7e4b-405b-34c8-bd01-13a9ef463b10", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1"}, {"id": "46e298ea-f91c-38c3-8751-24095bde4602", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fc8943886629e26de34867db302c74d465510826 <dac69d1b76049d7e5f565089a6a7f4502a85b9de"}, {"id": "594dd16b-86b2-3ed0-a03d-0034055bc290", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12.10 <6.12.114"}, {"id": "70d9c2d7-664a-313d-84a1-e61eb86edd21", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.42"}, {"id": "7268a158-8ae0-3d7d-8f82-ff145c2cab13", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6df90c02bae468a3a6110bafbc659884d0c4966c <430a05cb926f6bdf53e81460a2c3a553257f3f61"}, {"id": "85449a1d-c7b4-39dc-b0e8-eafb379e4d97", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6df90c02bae468a3a6110bafbc659884d0c4966c <d47281b9a4472cfd73122393e79fbe76b651e46a"}, {"id": "9a3ccf85-c333-34eb-b09a-37b64d21b706", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "acdd401f-e4e2-3edc-8020-2d221902c236", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.1.125 <6.2"}, {"id": "cbec3712-24b6-36b0-8e8c-a1de1c0ff829", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.13"}, {"id": "d64b5711-3d64-30d0-ab7b-a6c62fc86eec", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0.7"}, {"id": "e268b895-3da3-31d6-b44c-69e73c4bda5d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6.72 <6.6.160"}, {"id": "e77e79f5-8717-34dd-a2ca-572fe013fe09", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "ec4f80e1-30ff-373f-ac30-743072719508", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6df90c02bae468a3a6110bafbc659884d0c4966c <3d1b4e2d8ac0a1a1390a117f61ce0ca1c47e3bcb"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "c5368900-1b0c-3f15-9420-f7e432fca8f3", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}